  "count_definition": "Actual executions across both SDKs, paging modes and P/E cores, not unique inputs. Focused runs are excluded. Existing single shifts/rotates and other instruction families have separate regression counts.",
  "undefined_state_contract": "DoubleShiftUndefined permits only CF/PF/AF/ZF/SF/OF. Only masked word counts above 16 consume Result and all arithmetic Flags; count equal to the width is defined. Other nonzero counts consume only AF and, above one, OF. Zero counts preserve the operand and all flags. Upper destination words and unrelated flags never consume the image.",
  "native_observation": "X86LegacyShiftNativeFixture shares one W^X register probe between single and double shifts. The producer supplies only undefined slices observed from a separate host instruction of the same count encoding, using the actual original operand inputs, and restores host flags. No KVM result, defined bit, memory change or exception result is fed back. The main oracle compares original protected instruction GPRs, flags, CR2, selected operand/stack/frame bytes and successful operand PTE A/D effects. This is not a portable undefined-state policy.",
  "memory_contract": "Zero and undefined counts retain writable-segment, page and alignment checks. Register source and CL are captured before destination writes. Prepared read/modify/write plans retain native write-fault bits and original restart state. Cross-page faults publish no partial operand. Original handlers repair PTEs and retry without host register repair. The unchanged ordered page walker may differ from this CPU on faulting-walk A bits; exact faulting-walk A/D identity remains outside this qualification.",
  "implementation": "X86LegacyScalarEncoding authenticates the four opcode forms and exact extents. X86LegacyScalarExecution computes defined results with a 64-bit concatenation and original input snapshots. Independent unit tests use single-bit transfers and arbitrary undefined images, including a full defined word count and the next undefined count.",
  "retained_diagnostics": "The first segment matrix failed in undefined OF for SHLD word [SS:BX],DX,CL with nonflat data segments and count 16. The probe used the initialized DS operand while SS actually referenced the zero-filled base-zero page. The producer now uses that original SS input. The original failed log, source snapshot and binary are retained under first-ss-observer-mismatch. Production execution was unchanged by the probe repair. The alias matrix was also expanded so CL aliases exercise their selected count and memory sources can coincide with the address base. The added single-shift SS regression reproduced the same bad input on E. After fixing inputs, P still differed in undefined OF for ROL byte memory,2. An independent host probe confirmed that this P core preserves OF for its register form but computes a different image for its memory form; the E core agreed across forms. The final observer therefore executes the same register/memory form, with an independent scratch slot for memory. The failed P replay and intentionally canceled r6 E replay are retained and excluded from successful totals.",
